   <text>
      <body>
         <!-- Saving a template to paste for every calendar sheet to keep consistent formatting 
         <div type="calendarSheet" n="">
            <fw place="top-center" hand="#print"><hi rend="bold"><lb/>COPYRIGHT <date when="1908"
                     >1908</date>, BY <lb/>FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. <lb/>NEW BRITAIN, CONN.</hi></fw>
            <milestone unit="line" rend="dotted-line"/>
            <dateline hand="#printFancy"><date when=""/><hi rend="drop cap"><lb/>MONTH
               DAY,1909. <lb/>WEEKDAY</dateline>
            <figure place="center" hand="#multiMedia">
               <figDesc></figDesc>

               <ab hand="#blackPen" rend="cursive"><lb/><lb/><hi
                     hand="#redPen"></hi></ab>
            </figure>
         </div>
         -->

         <div type="calendarSheet" n="1">
            <fw place="top-center" hand="#print"><hi rend="bold"><lb/>COPYRIGHT <date when="1908"
                     >1908</date>, BY <lb/>FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. <lb/>NEW BRITAIN, CONN.</hi></fw>
            <milestone unit="line" rend="dotted-line"/>
            <dateline hand="#printFancy"><date when="1909-02-16"/><hi rend="drop cap"><add
                     hand="#redPen" rend="Mary Behrend colored the letter 'F' in red"
                  ><lb/>F</add></hi>ebruary 16,1909. <lb/>Tuesday</dateline>
            <figure place="center" hand="#multiMedia">
               <figDesc> Drawing of Mr. Behrend catching a bed bug from their white bed</figDesc>

               <ab hand="#blackPen" rend="cursive"><lb/>Mr. Behrend finds a<lb/>bed bug!<lb/><hi
                     hand="#redPen">I wonder if you have found many lately!</hi></ab>
            </figure>
         </div>
         <div type="sheet" n="2">
            <fw place="top-center" hand="#print"><hi rend="bold"><lb/>COPYRIGHT <date when="1908"
                     >1908</date>, BY <lb/>FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. <lb/>NEW BRITAIN, CONN.</hi></fw>
            <milestone unit="line" rend="dotted-line"/>
            <dateline hand="#printFancy"><hi rend="drop cap"><date when="1909-03-17"/><add
                     hand="#greenPen" rend="Mary Behrend colored the letter 'M' in green"
                     ><lb/>M</add></hi>arch 17,1909.<lb/>Wednesday <lb/>St. Patrick's Day</dateline>
            <figure place="below dateline" hand="#multiMedia">
               <figDesc n="1">Two green shamrocks on opposite edges of the sheet with two black ink
                  snake doodles between them towards the center of the page</figDesc>
               <ab hand="#blackPen" rend="printed writing"><lb/>ST. PATRICK WAS A USEFUL
                  SAINT<lb/>HE FRIGHTENED ALL THE SNAKES AWAY-<lb/>I WISH HE'D TRY HIS ART ON <hi
                     rend="underlined">SMOKE</hi><lb/>AROUND THE HAMMERMILL SOME DAY!</ab>
               <figDesc n="2">Green shamrok with a drawing in black ink of the Hammermil building to
                  the right of it</figDesc>

               <ab hand="#redPen" rend="cursive"><lb/>The Hammermill really <emph rend="underlined"
                        ><gap reason="illegible"/>
                     <!-- attempting to mark my uncertainty with the reading of this sentence, the letters in the words are quite hard to make out -->
                     <unclear reason="illegible">lucky!</unclear></emph></ab>
            </figure>
         </div>
         <div type="calendarSheet" n="3">
            <fw place="top-center" hand="#print"><hi rend="bold"><lb/>COPYRIGHT <date when="1908"
                     >1908</date>, BY <lb/>FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. <lb/>NEW BRITAIN, CONN.</hi></fw>
            <milestone unit="line" rend="dotted-line"/>
            <dateline hand="#printFancy"><date when="1909-03-08"/><hi rend="drop cap"><lb/><add
                     hand="#redPen" rend="Mary Behrend colored the letter 'M' in red"
               >M</add></hi>arch 8,1909. <lb/>Monday</dateline>
            <figure place="center" hand="#multiMedia">
               <figDesc>Large red question mark</figDesc>

               <ab hand="#blackPen" rend="cursive"><lb/>Perhaps this is<lb/>the day, this is<lb/>the
                  day, this i<lb/>think or will be<lb/>later. Love, M.</ab>
            </figure>
         </div>
         <div type="calendarSheet" n="4">
            <fw place="top-center" hand="#print"><hi rend="bold"><lb/>COPYRIGHT <date when="1908"
                     >1908</date>, BY <lb/>FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. <lb/>NEW BRITAIN, CONN.</hi></fw>
            <milestone unit="line" rend="dotted-line"/>
            <dateline hand="#printFancy"><date when="1909-02-17"/><hi rend="drop cap"><lb/><add
                     hand="#redPen" rend="Mary Behrend colored the letter 'F' in red"
               >F</add></hi>ebruary 17,1909. <lb/>Wednesday</dateline>
            <figure place="center" hand="#multiMedia">
               <ab hand="#blackPen" rend="cursive"><l>Each morning <emph rend="underlined"
                        >very</emph> early</l><l>When all is dark &amp; still</l><l>Ernst gets <emph
                        rend="underlined">up</emph> in inkey blackness</l><l>to work at
                     Hammermill</l><l>I really think he's very good</l><l>to get up when it's
                     dark</l><l>for this he says he doesn't <gap reason="illegible"/></l><l><hi
                        hand="#redPen"><gap reason="illegible"/> is it still dark when you
                        arise?</hi></l><hi hand="#redPen"/></ab>
            </figure>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
